# Line-ending policy.
#
# Why this file exists: with `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows, Git stores LF
# but checks these files out as CRLF. Terraform then reads the CRLF working
# copy into its heredoc string values while the remote state holds LF, so
# `terraform plan` reported every line of three helm_release values as
# changed — identical text on both sides. That made the plan permanently
# non-empty, which meant "plan is clean" could never be used as a drift
# signal and real drift (the Step 1.5.6 #7 Alertmanager route) hid inside
# the whitespace noise.
#
# Anything consumed by Terraform, Kubernetes, Helm, or a Linux shell is
# pinned to LF regardless of host OS. PowerShell scripts stay CRLF.

*.tf      text eol=lf
*.tfvars  text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.sh      text eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts keep CRLF.
*.ps1     text eol=crlf
*.bat     text eol=crlf

# Never munge binaries.
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.gz      binary
